[O — THE CHORUS BOUNDARY, MEASURED ON THE OUTPUT, ON EVERY TYPE]
      🔴 fb422. ROSTER §0 claimed the boundary was "enforced in the DSP, not in
      prose" and that this section asserted it. It did not: it measured nV_, a
      published integer, on Throng and Twofold — i.e. NOT on `Twin`, whose line count
      is a different expression entirely, and NOT on `Steady`. Both of those are
      fixed here, and the count is cross-checked against the OUTPUT.

      What a chorus IS, per CONTRACT §4: ONE audible cyclic voice pair. Failing that
      needs either (a) more than one pair of copies, or (b) copies that do not
      CYCLE. Every Type is checked against both, and each must satisfy at least one
      — stated as a disjunction because it genuinely is one, not to make a cell pass.

      1 · the copy count at the Voices FLOOR, per Type and per Character that
          claims a count in its own name:
